'' RUN: abort( ) with an ON ERROR handler installed: the handler runs and ENDs with 3. The
'' thread's error context exists (ON ERROR made it), so TK-004's handler takes the throw path,
'' and lowers its re-entry guard first. (fbc-modern loops on "before" here until it crashes.)
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/signal-onerror.bas -o tests/codegen/signalonerror.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/signalonerror.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: before
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: caught
